  "body": "Implement native AI provider transport, secret handling, and transport-level offline enforcement in `crates/app`.\n\n## Scope\n- Gate native sockets, threads, and OS keychain calls under `#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]` so `crates/ui` continues to build on `wasm32` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell_web.rs`).\n- Support public cloud endpoints (`https://` only):\n  - Anthropic Messages API\n  - OpenAI Chat Completions and Responses APIs (GPT and Codex models)\n  - Google Gemini `generateContent` API\n- Support OpenAI-compatible local endpoints (`localhost` / `127.0.0.1` / `[::1]`):\n  - Ollama (`http://localhost:11434/v1` plus `/api/show` capability probe)\n  - Unsloth Studio (`http://127.0.0.1:8888`)\n  - LM Studio (`http://localhost:1234/v1`)\n  - `llama.cpp` `llama-server` (`--jinja`)\n- Store API keys only in the OS keychain (`keyring` crate) or environment variables (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`). Never write secrets to `prefs.json` (`crates/app/src/prefs.rs`) or project files. Reject plain `http://` when sending keys off localhost.\n- Add `ai_offline_only` to `ViewPrefs` in `crates/app/src/prefs.rs` and reject all non-loopback hosts inside the HTTP client before opening a socket.\n- Use only public provider specifications and update `assets/ui/LICENSES.md` for new third-party crates.\n\nDone means: Fake loopback HTTP server tests verify every provider wire format and Ollama capability detection, `prefs.json` stores zero keys, offline mode blocks non-loopback hosts, and `cargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown` builds cleanly.\n\nPart of #1773\n",
